<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Seven numbers with given median quartiles and mean</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Write seven whole numbers, smallest first, so that the median is \({@m@}\), the lower quartile is \({@q1@}\), the upper quartile is \({@q3@}\) and the mean is \({@m@}\).</p><p>Type the seven numbers in square brackets, separated by commas, for example <code>[3,5,8,9,12,14,20]</code>.</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>For seven values in order, \(n + 1 = 8\), so the median is at position \(8/2 = 4\), \(Q_1\) at \(8/4 = 2\) and \(Q_3\) at \(3 \times 8/4 = 6\). These positions are whole numbers, so fix the 2nd, 4th and 6th numbers as \({@q1@}\), \({@m@}\) and \({@q3@}\).</p><p>Choose the 1st, 3rd and 5th numbers to keep the list in order, for example \({@q1-1@}\), \({@m-1@}\) and \({@m+1@}\). Seven numbers with mean \({@m@}\) add to \(7 \times {@m@} = {@7*m@}\), so the 7th number is what is left: \({@7*m@} - {@7*m-(m+2*a-b+1)@} = {@m+2*a-b+1@}\), which is at least \({@q3@}\), as it must be.</p><p>One answer is \({@ta@}\). Any list of whole numbers in order with these 2nd, 4th and 6th numbers and total \({@7*m@}\) is correct.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: construct-an-example pattern. b < a keeps the example's largest value at least Q3. Negative entries are invalid (not whole numbers), so a list such as [-178,22,30,30,30,32,244] does not score. Source: original. */
m: rand_with_step(24,36,1);
a: 5+rand(4);
b: 2+rand(a-2);
q1: m-a;
q3: m+b;
ta: [q1-1, q1, m-1, m, m+1, q3, m+2*a-b+1];
tsum: 7*m;
validate_seven(ex) := if listp(ex) and length(ex)=7 and every(lambda([v], integerp(ev(v,simp)) and is(ev(v,simp)>=0)), ex) then "" else "Type exactly seven whole numbers in square brackets, separated by commas.";
/* test values */
t3: [q1-1,q1,m-2,m-1,m+1,q3,m+2*a-b+1];
t4: [q1-2,q1-1,m-1,m,m+1,q3,m+2*a-b+3];
t5: [q1-1,q1,m-1,m,m+1,q3,m+2*a-b+2];
trev: reverse(ta);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
